# ⭐ OPIc Sample Answer - Day20

One thing I worked hard to achieve was improving my English.

I wanted to become more comfortable speaking English because I thought it would be useful for my future.

At first, I found it difficult to study consistently.

However, I decided to study a little every day instead of studying for a long time only once or twice a week.

I learned new vocabulary, practiced grammar, and also tried speaking English out loud.

As a result, I became more comfortable expressing my thoughts in English.

I still have a lot to learn, but I feel proud of the progress I've made.
